|name2 = Aoshi Shinomori CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Aoshi Shinomori CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Aoshi Shinomori is a below-average Anti-Angel and Anti-Floating Crowd Controller, his 70% uptime [[Freeze]] at a 50% chance making his effective uptime closer to 35%. Many Floating and Angel enemies boast high stats and devastating pushing power, his range allows him to stay a safe distance away from said enemies. There is potential for fast enemies such as [[Angelic Gory]] to push into his blindspot easily, in which specialist meatshields such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] are recommended. His DPS is quite low, as his main function is Crowd Control, and his HP is average for a Unit with his role. His Strong Against ability doesn't do much for him because of said average stats, only making him okay against his traits when it comes to HP and DPS.

Aoshi is commonly compared to [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Talented Sanzo Cat]] due to them sharing the same Target-Traits and roles. Talented Sanzo Cat effectively deals with most Floating and Angel enemies that Aoshi also does okay against. Being an Uber, Aoshi is naturally less accessible as a Unit, and also harder to replace if he ends up dying when compared to Talented Sanzo. A single Talented Sanzo's [[Slow]] and [[Weaken]] being near an effective 100% uptime makes Aoshi's Freeze look quite lack-luster in comparison. Aoshi does have the advantage against a select few enemies Sanzo is ineffective against, mostly due to Aoshi's superior standing and piercing range. Some threats where Aoshi is superior to Sanzo include [[Othom]], [[Winged Pigge]], and [[St. Dober]]. Because of his Crowd Control being Freeze instead of Slow, he also has an advantage against backliners with large standing ranges such as [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Cruel Angel Clionel]], with his [[Immune to Slow|Immunity to Slow]] also helping against these two enemies specifically.

Because of Aoshi's disappointing stats and below average performance in his very competitive niche, it's recommended to only use him at times where a Talented Sanzo or other relevant Floating and Angel Crowd Control Units prove ineffective.

